#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:1
msgid "Autotuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:3
msgid ""
"`cutile::tune` searches a declared space of kernel configurations, measures "
"each candidate with `cutile::bench`'s device-event timing, and persists both "
"the trials and the winner. It is gated behind the `experimental-tune` "
"feature, and the API may change between releases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:8
msgid "cutile = { version = \"...\", features = [\"experimental-tune\"] }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:12
msgid ""
"Use a closure to tune an individual kernel, or implement `Objective` to "
"measure a whole request. These synchronous interfaces and their resume logs "
"remain supported. The opt-in preparation pipeline below overlaps CPU "
"compilation with foreground GPU evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:17
msgid "Finding a good configuration under a time budget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:19
msgid ""
"Use Bayesian optimization (BO) with lookahead compilation when a full sweep "
"would take too long. BO uses measurements from this run to choose useful "
"next experiments; lookahead compiles future candidates while the GPU "
"evaluates the current one. With a budget shorter than a full sweep, this "
"explores only part of the declared space. The result is a tested candidate, "
"not proof of the global optimum. A small space may still be exhausted within "
"the budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:26
msgid ""
"From `cutile-rs/`, try the RMSNorm example with a 30-second tuning budget "
"and one preparation worker (the default lookahead):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:29
msgid ""
"cargo run --release -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features "
"experimental-tune -- --search bayes --workers 1 --budget-ms 30000 --seed 42\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:33
msgid ""
"To try more parallel compilation, change `--workers 1` to `--workers 4`. "
"This bounds the number of preparing or ready candidates, not concurrent GPU "
"measurements. More lookahead can hide slow compilation, but those candidates "
"are chosen before the latest results arrive and some may never be measured. "
"Compare with `--serial` and with `--search random` under the same budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:39
msgid "For your own workload, configure the pipeline and selector together:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:41
msgid ""
"use std::time::Duration;\n"
"use cutile::tune::pipeline::{BayesianOptions, BayesianSearch, Pipeline};\n"
"\n"
"let mut strategy = BayesianSearch::new(&configs, "
"BayesianOptions::default())?;\n"
"let pipeline = Pipeline::default()\n"
"    .workers(1)\n"
"    .budget(Duration::from_secs(30))\n"
"    .trial_limit(Duration::from_secs(10));\n"
"// Supply resolve/prepare/evaluate and paired-confirmation callbacks to\n"
"// pipeline.run_confirmed(...), as described below and in the example.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:54
msgid ""
"With one worker, B compiles while A is evaluated. A's result then informs "
"the choice of C, which compiles while B is evaluated. The strategy accounts "
"for pending candidates so it does not suggest the same experiment twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:58
msgid ""
"Use `run_confirmed` to compare finalists with a known incumbent; its default "
"reserves 25% of the same budget for fresh paired measurements. If "
"confirmation cannot finish, only an alternative that already completed every "
"required round can replace the incumbent. Otherwise `NotConfirmed` keeps the "
"incumbent and does not certify a replacement. Budgeting is cooperative: it "
"stops new work and bounds controlled stages, but an already-running GPU "
"operation or user callback can overrun. Application build time and the "
"example's fixture setup are outside the tuning budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:67
msgid "Preparing candidates in parallel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:69
msgid ""
"The `autotune` example checks RMSNorm outputs against a CPU reference and "
"verifies that its first launch reuses the prepared binary. Run it from the "
"`cutile-rs/` workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:73
msgid ""
"cargo run --release -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features "
"experimental-tune\n"
"# Compare more CPU workers with the same measurement protocol:\n"
"cargo run --release -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features "
"experimental-tune -- --workers 4 --budget-ms 30000\n"
"cargo run --release -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features "
"experimental-tune -- --serial\n"
"# Compare selection with the same worker count, budget and confirmation:\n"
"cargo run --release -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features "
"experimental-tune -- --search random --seed 42\n"
"cargo run --release -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features "
"experimental-tune -- --search grid\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:83
msgid ""
"`tune::pipeline::Pipeline` owns scheduling. Its three callbacks have "
"separate roles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:86
msgid ""
"`resolve` runs on the foreground thread. Resolve the actual launch metadata "
"with `.specialize_on(&stream)`, then call `.into_compile_job()` to capture "
"the target and compiler settings. This step can query the device and execute "
"input operations; do not move it into a preparation worker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:90
msgid ""
"`prepare` runs on CPU workers. `job.compile(control)` runs the Rust frontend "
"and assembler, producing a host-owned `PreparedKernel`. It does not load a "
"CUDA module or synchronize a CUDA stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:93
msgid ""
"`evaluate` runs on the foreground thread, one candidate at a time. Check the "
"artifact's key against the actual launch, call `prepared.install(control)`, "
"run a correctness check, then measure with `bench::do_bench_controlled`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:97
msgid ""
"Explicit installation is optional: an ordinary launch of the same "
"specialization joins an in-progress CPU compilation and loads the resulting "
"binary itself. Keep the `PreparedKernel` handle alive until that launch if "
"compilation has already finished. The example installs explicitly so it can "
"separately check that the subsequent launch leaves the installation counter "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:103
msgid ""
"Preparation and ordinary cache-miss launches share the same CPU compilation "
"registry. Whichever begins compilation first produces the binary; other "
"callers wait without compiling it again. Loading still occurs on a "
"foreground caller. Cancelling a waiter does not cancel another caller's "
"compilation. If the owner is cancelled or panics, a waiting caller with a "
"live budget can retry; compiler errors are reported and later attempts "
"remain retryable. Registry entries and CPU artifacts disappear when their "
"last caller releases them. This deduplicates overlapping work; it does not "
"add a permanent CPU binary cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:112
msgid ""
"One worker is the default: while A is evaluated, B compiles; after observing "
"A, the strategy selects C while B is evaluated. With `workers(k)`, at most k "
"candidates are preparing or ready in addition to the current evaluation. "
"More workers can improve throughput but also perturb short-kernel timings; "
"measure this tradeoff on your workload. `overlap(false)` supplies a "
"sequential comparison with the same callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:119
msgid ""
"`Strategy::suggest` sees completed observations, every pending index "
"(including the current evaluation), and remaining time. `observe` receives "
"each outcome. `RandomOrder::new(seed).with_initial([baseline_index])` "
"provides seeded sampling without replacement, exhausting the space when the "
"budget allows. Create a fresh strategy per run. Initial indices are "
"suggestions, not a guarantee of incumbent coverage. `GridOrder` visits the "
"declared order. The example defaults to the Bayesian selector described "
"below; the synchronous `Autotuner` still defaults to `GridSearch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:128
msgid ""
"The budget includes resolution, queueing, preparation, loading, correctness "
"checks and measurement. `trial_limit` gives resolution, preparation and "
"evaluation each a fresh active-stage allowance, always capped by the overall "
"run deadline. Time waiting in the scheduler's own queues counts against the "
"run budget, but not the stage limit; waiting inside a callback, including a "
"remote service queue, still consumes that callback's active-stage allowance. "
"The example's fixture and CPU-reference setup happen before the run clock "
"starts. Expired deadlines stop dispatch and exclude late measurements from "
"scoring. The assembler process can be killed and reaped; frontend passes and "
"benchmark repetitions check cancellation between stages. Arbitrary "
"callbacks, CUDA calls and running GPU kernels cannot be forcibly "
"interrupted. Returning waits for outstanding workers, so this is a "
"cooperative deadline, not a hard wall-clock guarantee. Interrupted assembler "
"runs remove their bytecode and temporary intermediates after reaping the "
"process; ordinary compiler failures still retain the bytecode named in their "
"diagnostic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:144
msgid ""
"Explicit `Failure::invalid` outcomes and source-located frontend rejections "
"(`JITError::Located`, converted through `Failure::from`) mark a candidate "
"invalid. Unclassified compiler/driver errors still stop the run. Return a "
"measured `Trial` on success: legacy invalid trials also represent non-finite "
"timings, so the pipeline treats them as infrastructure errors. Timeouts and "
"cancellations are unscored. Infrastructure errors remain `Infrastructure` "
"and stop the run even if a deadline or cancellation happened first, "
"including when collecting results from draining workers. Other late failures "
"are classified as `TimedOut` or `Cancelled`, with their original diagnostic "
"retained in `Failure::reason`. Neither outcome becomes a usable measurement. "
"Generic compiler/driver errors default to infrastructure errors because they "
"may reflect the environment rather than the candidate. The caller can "
"classify a known candidate-specific rejection explicitly. Observations "
"include separate stage durations; an unvisited stage is `None`, and "
"overlapping stage times must not be summed as elapsed wall time. Evaluation "
"time includes loading, checks and measurement, rather than pretending those "
"costs were measured separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:161
msgid ""
"**`run().best_observed` is provisional.** Use `run_confirmed` below, or "
"independently compare finalists with your incumbent before applying a "
"result. An incomplete search has no best observed result. The synchronous "
"resume-log schema is unchanged; the pipeline does not read or write it. "
"Store observations with workload, source and toolchain provenance if you "
"need an audit record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:167
msgid ""
"Prepared artifacts are bounded by the pipeline, but installed modules retain "
"the existing global cache lifetime. Automatic eviction is deliberately "
"avoided: other streams may still be using a specialization. See cache "
"management below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:171
msgid "Bayesian selection with a neutral starting point"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:173
msgid ""
"`BayesianSearch` fits a small Gaussian process to **current-run log "
"latencies** and scores every unvisited configuration by expected "
"improvement. It can spend a measurement on a promising uncertain region "
"rather than simply trying the lowest predicted latency. This is intended for "
"small finite spaces with costly evaluations, not millions of candidates. "
"Fitting is cubic in the number of observations, and scoring the finite list "
"adds work for each candidate. Model work is included in the budget and "
"checks the deadline between fit rows and candidate scores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:182
msgid ""
"use cutile::tune::pipeline::{BayesianOptions, BayesianSearch, "
"ParameterScale};\n"
"\n"
"let options = BayesianOptions {\n"
"    seed: 42,\n"
"    scales: [(\"BLOCK_SIZE\".into(), ParameterScale::Log2)].into(),\n"
"    ..Default::default()\n"
"};\n"
"let mut strategy = BayesianSearch::new(&configs, "
"options)?.with_initial([0])?;\n"
"// Pass &mut strategy to Pipeline::run_confirmed as below.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:194
msgid ""
"Without `with_initial` or explicit prior offsets, every configuration has "
"the same prior mean and marginal uncertainty; a seeded tie-break selects the "
"first candidate. Integer axes default to linear normalization, positive tile "
"sizes can opt into logarithmic scaling, and strings are categorical. Integer "
"category IDs can also use `Categorical`. Every configuration must declare "
"the same keys and parameter types. The Matérn 5/2 kernel, length scale and "
"observation noise are fixed explicit settings in `BayesianOptions`, rather "
"than hyperparameters fit from a handful of samples. These defaults are "
"starting assumptions, not a claim that this model is best for every tuning "
"space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:204
msgid ""
"Optional `prior_log_offsets` give weak preferences by configuration ID. For "
"example, `-0.1` encodes an expected latency about 10% below the common "
"baseline. Offsets are limited to magnitude `ln(2)`, leave initial "
"uncertainty unchanged, and never add observations. Hardware-informed hints "
"must be supplied explicitly; the tuner does not invent architecture rules, "
"call an LLM, or train offline. The default remains neutral. If using "
"previous tuning runs to construct hints or initial candidate suggestions, "
"verify the kernel, parameter meanings, workload, GPU and compiler first. Do "
"not insert old timings into current-run observations. Automatic history "
"retrieval and cross-kernel transfer are not implemented, and resume "
"provenance checks are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:215
msgid ""
"Pending configurations are temporarily conditioned at their predicted means, "
"reducing redundant exploration while another candidate is compiling or being "
"measured. They cannot improve the measured incumbent. Expected improvement "
"uses the best posterior mean among valid measured points; this is a plug-in "
"treatment of noise, not an integrated noisy-EI algorithm. Invalid and timed-"
"out points use the same predicted-mean conditioning to reduce repeated "
"exploration around failures. This reduces acquisition uncertainty without "
"changing the predicted mean or incumbent; it is a search heuristic, not "
"evidence of a measured latency or a learned probability of validity. "
"Cancelled and infrastructure-failed points receive no such penalty. All "
"failed trials remain excluded as latency targets. Known rejected candidate "
"indices are excluded; the first implementation does not predict the validity "
"of unseen configurations. A numerical failure falls back to seeded random "
"and increments `numerical_fallbacks()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:229
msgid ""
"The implementation uses standard GP regression equations with Cholesky "
"solves, checked against independent scikit-learn/SciPy fixtures. It adds no "
"ML runtime dependency. Compare it with seeded random and grid under the "
"**same elapsed-time budget**, including compilation, correctness checks and "
"confirmation. Small spaces that fit the budget can be exhausted by any "
"strategy; there is no claim that a model always wins. The existing "
"`Strategy` interface also permits a different selector without changing "
"compilation or measurement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:237
msgid "Screening and confirming a replacement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:239
msgid ""
"The RMSNorm example uses `Pipeline::run_confirmed` with "
"`ConfirmationOptions::new(incumbent_index)`. It requires a total `budget` "
"and adds a fourth, foreground callback to the preparation pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:243
msgid ""
"let policy = ConfirmationOptions::new(0);\n"
"let result = pipeline.run_confirmed(\n"
"    &configs, &mut strategy, &policy,\n"
"    resolve, prepare,\n"
"    |config, prepared, bench_options, control| { /* check, screen -> Trial "
"*/ },\n"
"    |incumbent, candidate, bench_options, control| {\n"
"        // Check the incumbent normally: an error here must stop "
"confirmation.\n"
"        // Mark only candidate-specific invalidity with\n"
"        // .map_err(Failure::for_candidate), then return aligned "
"measurements\n"
"        // from bench::do_bench_paired_controlled(...).\n"
"    },\n"
")?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:258
msgid ""
"The default policy screens with at most 50 timed repetitions and reserves "
"25% of the total budget for confirmation. Screening may finish sooner if the "
"declared space is exhausted. After **all preparation workers have joined and "
"queued artifacts have been dropped**, it compares the four best measured "
"alternatives with the incumbent in three fresh rounds. The incumbent is "
"compared even if it was never screened. Both arms must pass fresh "
"correctness checks in the callback, and a known invalid incumbent is not "
"used. Attribute candidate-only failures with "
"`.map_err(Failure::for_candidate)` around that arm's checks: this converts "
"`Invalid` into `InvalidCandidate`, without relabeling infrastructure errors "
"or interruptions. A generic `Invalid` from the paired callback remains "
"ambiguous and stops confirmation because it may concern the incumbent. Never "
"wrap the whole comparison or incumbent checks with `for_candidate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:271
msgid ""
"No background preparation runs during these comparisons; callers must also "
"keep unrelated GPU work away from the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:274
msgid ""
"`do_bench_paired_controlled` alternates A/B then B/A ordering, with aligned "
"raw samples and cancellation/deadline checks between arms. A comparison "
"cannot return an unmatched pair as a successful measurement. The pipeline's "
"`trial_limit` applies to each paired comparison, including its correctness "
"checks. Confirmation uses the original overall deadline, not a new budget. "
"As with screening, an uninterruptible callback or GPU operation can still "
"overrun it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:281
msgid ""
"For each pair the improvement is `1 - candidate_time / incumbent_time`. By "
"default, the lower quartile of those improvements must exceed 2% in "
"**every** round. Among qualifying candidates, the result selects the largest "
"worst-round median improvement. This is a conservative, configurable "
"repeatability heuristic, not a confidence interval or a universal 2% noise "
"threshold. Calibrate the margin, repetitions and round count for your "
"kernels and hardware; the defaults do not guarantee an optimal choice. "
"Finalist order reverses on alternate rounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:289
msgid ""
"`ConfirmedOutput` includes screening observations, raw paired samples, "
"failures, the incumbent, the selected configuration and one of three "
"statuses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:292
msgid "`Improved`: a replacement passed the configured confirmation rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:293
msgid ""
"`NoImprovement`: every shortlisted alternative completed its comparisons, "
"but none passed the improvement rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:295
msgid ""
"`NotConfirmed`: insufficient valid candidates, failed checks, cancellation "
"or insufficient time. The selected configuration remains the supplied "
"incumbent; this status does **not** certify that the incumbent passed "
"validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:299
msgid ""
"Every selected replacement must complete all of its own required rounds, "
"with all correctness checks passing. An `InvalidCandidate` or candidate-"
"local timeout disqualifies only that candidate. Other finalists can "
"continue, and a later budget/cancellation cutoff can retain the best already "
"fully confirmed candidate; a partial leader never wins. "
"`ConfirmedOutput.failure` may therefore contain a timeout/cancellation "
"diagnostic alongside `Improved`; per-candidate errors remain in "
"`confirmations`. Infrastructure errors and incumbent/ambiguous correctness "
"errors stop confirmation without recommending a replacement, even after "
"another candidate completed its rounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:309
msgid ""
"Previous screening times and model predictions never count as fresh "
"confirmation evidence. A questionable correctness test should be "
"investigated separately; these rules do not waive failed tests or select by "
"correctness pass percentage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:313
msgid ""
"To save the example's observations and raw confirmation samples, pass `--"
"evidence NEW_FILE`. It creates a new JSON file without overwriting an "
"existing one. It includes the strategy settings and declared configurations. "
"Record source revision, GPU and toolkit alongside it; this example file is "
"evidence, not a provenance-checked resume log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:319
msgid "Declaring a space and running the search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:321
msgid ""
"A configuration is a set of named integer or string parameters; the space is "
"the list of configurations. Only `configs` and the terminal `run` are "
"required. The rest of the builder is optional: `prune` filters candidates, "
"`budget` bounds wall-clock, `log` makes the run resumable, and `require` "
"declares incumbents the search must cover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:327
msgid ""
"let configs: Vec<Config> = [16i64, 32, 64, 128]\n"
"    .into_iter()\n"
"    .map(|bn| Config::new([(\"BN\", ParamValue::Int(bn))]))\n"
"    .collect();\n"
"\n"
"let output = Autotuner::new(\"fmha_decode\")\n"
"    .configs(configs)\n"
"    .prune(|c| c.int(\"BN\").unwrap() <= pp)\n"
"    .require(vec![shipping_config])\n"
"    .budget(Duration::from_secs(300))\n"
"    .arch(\"sm_100\") // record the arch; a resume from another arch is "
"refused\n"
"    .log(\"fmha_decode.trials.jsonl\")\n"
"    .run(&stream, |stream, config| {\n"
"        // The setup closure is yours: read the config, build the kernel's\n"
"        // composed launcher for it, run it once as a correctness gate, and\n"
"        // return the closure to be timed. Err(..) records the candidate as\n"
"        // invalid and the search continues.\n"
"        let bn = config.int(\"BN\").unwrap();\n"
"        let mut launch = move |stream: &Arc<Stream>| {\n"
"            fmha_decode(out.partition([1, bn as i32]), &q, &k, &v)\n"
"                .generics(generics_for(bn))\n"
"                .sync_on(stream)\n"
"        };\n"
"        launch(&stream)?;\n"
"        Ok(launch)\n"
"    })?;\n"
"let best: Config = output.best.expect(\"a winner\");\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:357
msgid ""
"The two best candidates are compared in a paired A/B runoff to account for "
"clock and temperature drift. A finalist that fails setup forfeits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:360
msgid ""
"Every `require`d configuration must belong to the search space. These "
"configurations are measured first, before the budget can cut off the search. "
"The winner must match or beat each of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:364
msgid ""
"Trial logs record the tuner name and a hash of the search space. A log from "
"a different tuner or space is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:368
msgid "Measuring a full request with `Objective`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:370
msgid ""
"When the objective is end-to-end (tokens per second, request latency), the "
"library cannot own the launch. Implement `Objective` instead: `configs()` "
"exposes the space, `measure(index)` applies one candidate at engine scope "
"and returns a `Trial` built with `Trial::measured` or `Trial::invalid`, and "
"`budget_remaining()` reports what is left. `Autotuner::run_objective` then "
"provides the same trial logging, resume, and `require` coverage as the "
"closure path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:378
msgid ""
"let mut objective = EngineObjective::new(engine, configs);\n"
"let output = Autotuner::new(\"engine_prefill\")\n"
"    .arch(current_arch) // e.g. \"sm_100\"; resume refuses a foreign-arch "
"log\n"
"    .log(\"prefill.trials.jsonl\")\n"
"    .require(vec![current_default])\n"
"    .run_objective(&mut objective)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:387
msgid ""
"This path has no paired runoff: the library cannot re-time an engine "
"objective through its bench closures. `Output::best` is the best sequential "
"median. The caller can re-measure finalists together to check for drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:391
msgid ""
"Serialized `Trial` records remain compatible across cuTile upgrades. An "
"incompatible change increments the log schema version, and `TrialLog::open` "
"rejects the old schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:396
msgid "Committing winners"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:398
msgid ""
"A `tune::Record` persists winners so production loads them instead of re-"
"searching: one JSON file per kernel, written by `save` and committed next to "
"the code it tunes. The file holds a provenance header (kernel name, source "
"hash, cutile version, `tileiras` fingerprint, architecture, search-space "
"hash) and one entry per shape-class bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:404
msgid ""
"use cutile::tune::{L2Key, Record, RecordEntry, Workspace};\n"
"\n"
"// After tuning: `winner` is the winning Trial, `best` its Config\n"
"// (`output.best`), and `launcher` the kernel's composed builder applied\n"
"// with `best`'s values — the same call expression production dispatches.\n"
"let TrialState::Measured { median_ms, reps, .. } = winner.state else {\n"
"    unreachable!(\"the winner was measured\");\n"
"};\n"
"let mut record = Record::new(&workspace);\n"
"record.insert(RecordEntry {\n"
"    bucket: \"tg<=512\".into(),\n"
"    config: best,\n"
"    median_ms,\n"
"    samples: reps,\n"
"    l2_key: Some(L2Key::current(launcher.l2_cache_key()?)),\n"
"});\n"
"record.save(&path)?;\n"
"\n"
"// In production: load, verified against the running workspace.\n"
"let (record, warnings) = Record::load_verified(&path, &workspace, |entry| {\n"
"    Ok(Some(specialize_for(&entry.config)?.l2_cache_key()?))\n"
"})?;\n"
"let entry = record.get(\"tg<=512\");\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:430
msgid ""
"A bucket is a plain string label, matched exactly by `Record::get`; the "
"predicate that decides which bucket a runtime shape falls into lives in the "
"consumer's dispatch code, and the record only stores the label. `median_ms` "
"and `samples` are the winner's measured median latency and the number of "
"timed reps behind it — provenance for a human reading the committed file, "
"not inputs to verification. The `l2_key` is the winner's persistent-cache "
"key, computed from the composed builder without compiling or launching "
"(`.l2_cache_key()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:439
msgid ""
"`load_verified` rejects a record if its kernel, architecture, source hash, "
"or search space differs from the running workspace. It also recomputes each "
"entry's cache key to check the kernel's dependencies and toolchain. Changes "
"that affect only timing produce warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:444
msgid "Warming and managing the kernel cache during sweeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:446
msgid ""
"Call `.compile()` on the same builder used for `.execute` or `.sync_on` to "
"warm the specialization that will run. `api::meta` tensors supply shape and "
"dtype without device allocation or kernel launches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:450
msgid ""
"my_module::my_kernel(api::meta::<f32>(&[64, 64]).sync()?.partition([16, "
"16]), ...)\n"
"    .generics(generics)\n"
"    .compile_options(opts)\n"
"    .compile()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:457
msgid ""
"Tuning sweeps and long-running serving engines can accumulate many "
"specializations, and each cached kernel holds device memory. The in-memory "
"kernel cache is intentionally unbounded. The `unsafe` functions "
"`clear_kernel_cache()`, `evict_kernel(&key)`, and `retain_kernels(pred)` in "
"`cutile::tile_kernel` are available without any Cargo feature. They remove "
"entries, releasing each module's device memory when its last holder drops. "
"These functions are `unsafe`: synchronize every stream that may still be "
"running a cached kernel before evicting it. Between tuning trials or while a "
"serving engine is idle, callers can evict and then reload the needed "
"specializations. The autotuning API in `cutile::tune` still requires "
"`experimental-tune`."
msgstr ""
